  "result": "I've written the revised record to `record.jsonl`. It hasn't been validated or gated yet; the harness does that next. The two failing witnesses came from the record, not the Lean, and I changed the record to fix them.\n\n- **branch_1 (expected not_applicable, got unknown):** This run's reading puts no road-user class under the tour bus, shuttle bus or limo groupings (`DEF-LVMC-11-02-150::tour_bus`, `DEF-LVMC-11-02-150::shuttle_bus`, `DEF-LVMC-11-02-090::limo`). So whether a vehicle belongs to one of them is always unknown, and the planned \"tour bus, under thirty minutes → not_applicable\" case can't be reached by any faithful rule. I kept the groupings as they are rather than swap in `ru.tour_bus_or_limousine`. branch_1 is now a tour bus halting in a red zone of kind no_stopping. Because the zone isn't of kind tour_bus_loading, exception (2) fails whatever the bus's membership, so the expected verdict is violated. The s9 justification and the applicability text now say that unresolved membership leaves the exception unknown.\n- **branch_5 (expected not_applicable, got compliant):** The obligation holds the stopping definition's exclusions: a halt behind traffic, or a halt ordered by an officer or a device. A halt in a queue is therefore one the duty covers and meets. I changed branch_5's expected verdict to compliant to match the obligation as written, and kept the obligation itself. The obligation text now says this outright. The coder's extra device witnesses (branch_7 to branch_9, all compliant) agree with this.\n- **What else changed:** The three halt-duration exceptions, (2), (3) and (5), now require the subject to be at rest at the time. This makes the coder's choice part of the record. It can only change not_applicable to compliant for a moving vehicle, so it never changes the duty. I also gave the s3 and s18 narrowings their missing `kind: \"reading\"`.\n\nNone of the 18 spans needed withdrawing, and the record has no gaps.",
